Right, let me think about this honestly. I'm knackered after a ninety-minute commute, I'm training for a half marathon so I do care about what I eat, but I'm also not gonna be scared into submission by some gross medical photo while I'm just grabbing a snack. The calorie count thing—that actually matters to me because I can see if something fits my day, but graphic surgery photos would just wind me up and probably make me spite-buy the chocolate bar.

My gut reaction: calorie counts are genuinely useful information I'd actually look at. Graphic warnings feel preachy and patronizing—exactly the tone-deaf thing I already can't stand. No labelling is basically what we have now and it hasn't stopped me buying crap when I'm tired.

