Right, let me think about this honestly. Those graphic images with tumours and bleeding eyes—that's shock tactics, and it would probably wind me up more than make me think twice. I'd likely tune it out or feel annoyed at being lectured. The calorie counts on everything feel a bit pointless when I'm just grabbing a snack; I'm not sitting there doing maths. What *might* actually make a difference is if I could see at a glance what's genuinely lower-cal without the scaremongering, because then I could pick something less guilty-feeling without pretending I've gone health-conscious.

Honestly though? Most of this wouldn't change much. I know Doritos aren't a health food. Some days I'd pick them anyway because they're there or I fancy them. Some days I might grab a yoghurt. A warning label isn't going to stop me—I'm not an idiot who doesn't know crisps are bad for you.

